This graph shows the number of people who joined different activities at a social center in Melbourne from 2000 to 2020.
Overall, film clubs have stayed at the top of the chart. Table tennis has risen a lot after 2010, while amateur dramatics have fallen a lot. The other activities have changed less.
For the film club, the number of people was about 64 in 2000. It fell slowly to 60 in 2010, but then it rose again and reached about 66 in 2020. Table tennis has also changed a lot. It started at about 16 people in 2000 and rose to around 20 in 2005 and 2010. After that, it rose quickly and reached about 54 people in 2020.
Amateur dramatics rose a little from 26 to 28 between 2000 and 2005. However, it then fell and reached only about 6 people in 2020. Martial arts fluctuated between around 32 and 38 people throughout the period, showing little overall change. Musical performances have risen from 0 to about 18 people.
In conclusion, film clubs have stayed the most popular, while table tennis has risen the most. Meanwhile, many increases and decreases were observed after 2010.
