Nowadays, some people think competition at work, school, and in daily life makes people work harder, while others believe cooperation is more important for society. This essay will examine both perspectives before giving my own opinion. In my opinion, both views have some truth, but cooperation is more useful for society.

Those who support competition argue that it pushes people to improve themself. For example, students study harder when they compete for grades, and this shows that competition can create motivation.This is because competing against others creates clear, measurable goals that motivate people to work harder than they might otherwise.

On the other hand, others believe that cooperation allows people to achieve more than they could individually. This is because combining different people's skills and knowledge often produces better results than one person working alone. For example, in group projects at school, students who divide tasks according to their strengths tend to produce higher-quality work than students competing separately. This suggests that cooperation can be more effective than competition, particularly for complex tasks.

Admittedly, opponents may contend that competition also makes the workplace more efficient, because employees work hard to get promotions. However, they overlook that too much competition often causes stress and conflict between colleagues.

In conclusion, I believe cooperation is more beneficial than competition in most situations, because it creates a better environment for everyone in society and helps people work together happily.